6477001 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fcc02eae-d041-5167-9e1c-3e49457a629e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477001 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186315010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483515 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483518 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483515 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483515 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int x\\sqrt{x^{2} - 20}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nWork on an interval where $x^{2} - 20>0$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483515 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60241274-8490-524b-acba-fc74aea3d5e9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483515 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the $x$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(x^{2} - 20).$ But the derivative is $2 x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} - 20.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int x\\sqrt{x^{2} - 20}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u &=\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3}u^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\\\ &=\\frac{\\left(x^{2} - 20\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483524 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483514 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483524 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483524 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int x\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483524 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f11633ad-c3d3-53f8-93e6-d3a1d7d686df" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483524 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the $x$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(- x^{2} + 11).$ But the derivative is $- 2 x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=- x^{2} + 11.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=- 2 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int x\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=- \\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{3}\\,\\text{d}u &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{u^{4}}{4}+C\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{8}u^{4}+C\\\\ &=- \\frac{\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{4}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483525 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186068723.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483525 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "6d27df3f-00b8-523f-a56c-43a057ae4954" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485650 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186485652 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485650 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485650 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{3 x^{2} - 4}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485650 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d1f4346-0ddf-5d6f-9434-8141c2640699" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485650 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $u=x^{3} - 4 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3 x^{2} - 4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=(3 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3 x^{2} - 4}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\cdot (3 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\\left|x^{3} - 4 x\\right|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485653 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186068724.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485653 #edb/ref 